{
    // Standard custody wrap request.
    // Wraps a capability token: one whose mere presence among a transaction's inputs grants authority
    // somewhere else, such as a LithosDex provision's owner NFT (LD_Provision authorizes Claim and
    // Resize by "owner NFT in any input"). A batcher mints a receipt and moves the token into a
    // ZC_Standard_WrapVault, which releases it only to whoever burns the receipt. From then on the
    // token is never an input except in its unwrap, so a contract that lets third parties spend a box
    // holding the RECEIPT (an order fill, a liquidation, a vault pull or claim, an ask or lot refund)
    // lends them no authority. Put the receipt, never the raw token, into those contracts.
    // The owner is never assumed to be online after creating this box: any batcher runs the mint for
    // the mint fee.
    //
    // CONSTANTS
    // CONST_WRAP_VAULT_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of ZC_Standard_WrapVault
    //
    // TOKENS
    // tokens(0): (wrapped token, amount) - the only token allowed. Any amount, usually 1 (an NFT).
    //
    // REGISTERS
    // R4: Coll[Byte] - 32-byte owner script hash: receives the receipt, may cancel
    // R5: Long - mint batching fee, >= 2000000 nanoERG, paid to whoever runs the mint
    // R6: Coll[Coll[Byte]] - the receipt's EIP-4 (name, description, decimals), exactly 3 items.
    //   The owner's choice, fixed here so the minter cannot pick it.
    //
    // MINT (anyone; no context vars)
    // This box is the transaction's ONLY input. It holds the wrapped token, so any other input could
    // be a box the token has authority over (a LithosDex provision), spent in the same transaction.
    // That also means this box pays for everything: the vault, the receipt output and the mint fee.
    // INPUTS(0) = SELF: the receipt id is this box's id. Exactly 3 receipts are minted.
    // OUTPUTS(0): (receipt, 1) at tokens(0), at the owner script, at least 1000000 nanoERG,
    //   R4, R5, R6 = the three items of R6.
    // OUTPUTS(1): ZC_Standard_WrapVault with tokens exactly ((receipt, 2), the wrapped token and
    //   amount), at least 1000000 nanoERG, and no registers. The two outputs together receive at
    //   least SELF.value minus the mint fee. Value above 1000000 in the vault pays its refreshes
    //   (0.01 ERG each, about every two years), so a long-lived wrap should be funded for them.
    //
    // CANCEL
    // Nothing is minted, and a co-spent box guarded by the owner script releases this box. Only the
    // owner can build that transaction, so whatever else it spends is the owner's own doing. An owner
    // script that third parties can spend would expose the token while it waits here.
    //
    // VERIFYING A RECEIPT
    // Receipt id Y is genuine iff the box with id Y was spent under this exact script and constant
    // (supply the serialized box and check it hashes to Y, as ZC_Standard_LendOffer does for bonds).
    // The script then guarantees supply 3 with 2 locked in the vault, so "the box holding 2 units of
    // Y under ZC_Standard_WrapVault" is the wrap's state box: usable as a data input, and its
    // tokens(1) is the wrapped token and amount. This script does not check what that token is or
    // that it carries any authority: whoever values a receipt reads the token behind it. For a
    // LithosDex position that is the provision box naming the NFT in its R6, under the provision
    // guard of a pool the reader accepts, and that pool's box.

    def numTokenInOutputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        OUTPUTS.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) =>
            val count = b.tokens.fold(0L, { (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                if (t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
            })
            a + count
        })
    }

    val ownerHash = SELF.R4[Coll[Byte]].get
    val minted = numTokenInOutputs(SELF.id)

    if (minted > 0L) {
        val mintFee = SELF.R5[Long].get
        val metadata = SELF.R6[Coll[Coll[Byte]]].get
        if (metadata.size != 3 || OUTPUTS.size < 2 || SELF.tokens.size != 1) {
            sigmaProp(false)
        } else {
            val receiptOut = OUTPUTS(0)
            val vault = OUTPUTS(1)
            val wrapped = SELF.tokens(0)

            val termsValid =
                ownerHash.size == 32 &&
                mintFee >= 2000000L && mintFee <= SELF.value

            val mintValid =
                INPUTS.size == 1 &&
                SELF.id == INPUTS(0).id &&
                minted == 3L

            val receiptPaid =
                blake2b256(receiptOut.propositionBytes) == ownerHash &&
                receiptOut.value >= 1000000L &&
                receiptOut.tokens.size > 0 &&
                receiptOut.tokens(0)._1 == SELF.id && receiptOut.tokens(0)._2 == 1L &&
                receiptOut.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == metadata(0) &&
                receiptOut.R5[Coll[Byte]].get == metadata(1) &&
                receiptOut.R6[Coll[Byte]].get == metadata(2)

            val vaultValid =
                blake2b256(vault.propositionBytes) == CONST_WRAP_VAULT_HASH &&
                vault.value >= 1000000L &&
                vault.value + receiptOut.value >= SELF.value - mintFee &&
                vault.tokens == Coll((SELF.id, 2L), wrapped) &&
                vault.R4[Coll[Byte]].isDefined == false

            sigmaProp(termsValid && mintValid && receiptPaid && vaultValid)
        }
    } else {
        val ownerAuth = INPUTS.exists { (b: Box) =>
            b.id != SELF.id && blake2b256(b.propositionBytes) == ownerHash
        }
        sigmaProp(ownerAuth)
    }
}
